! I-Box 1 diagnostic program (docs/ja_ax1a_ibox-1.pdf p.51, routines
! WEN/WEN2/VEN, part of the "SIC-B,IND" test group) -- the smallest
! self-contained runnable fragment identified in this project's I-Box
! inventory pass (see docs/archival_inventory.md "6. The five I-Box
! diagnostic test programs"). Verifies that a VFL binary-unsigned Load
! correctly sets the RGZ (Result Greater-or-Zero) indicator for a
! nonzero unsigned value and the RZ (Result Zero) indicator for zero --
! exercises StretchALU.bsv's fieldToSM (forces sign=0 for unsigned
! mode) and StretchExecute.bsv's setResultIndicatorsF together, a
! genuinely behavioral check (not the type-width-guaranteed-safe shape
! archival_inventory.md's routine-1274 finding ruled out -- see there
! for why that candidate was rejected and this one picked instead).
!
! Source transcription note: the original routine's own instructions
! are reproduced faithfully --
!   WEN2  L%BU,64,8=,WEN7   -LOAD ONES     / BRGZZ,$+1.0 / BD,$
!   WEN   L%BU,64,8=,WEN6   -LOAD ZEROS    / BRZZ,$+1.0  / BD,$
!   VEN   L%BU,64,8=,WEN7                  / BRGZZ,$+1.0 / BD,$
! (WEN6/WEN7 are DD(BU,64,8) constants of all-zeros/all-ones,
! independently located and read at docs/ja_ax1a_ibox-1.pdf p.59) --
! but the pass/fail MECHANISM is deliberately NOT reproduced: the
! original's "BD,$" is a deliberate infinite-loop hang, meant for a
! human at the console to notice on real hardware, and its own
! continue/branch logic is wired through SIC (this model doesn't
! execute SIC's embedded branch -- see archival_inventory.md's
! "Verification" section). Reusing either would make this program hang
! in Bluesim on any failure with no observable signal. Instead: each
! check's PASS path writes a distinctive marker (100, via LVI -- an
! ImmIndex op that, per StretchExecute.bsv's ImmIndex arm, does NOT
! call setIndexResultIndicatorsF, so marker writes never disturb the
! RGZ/RZ state a later check still needs to read) into its own index
! register, pre-cleared to 0 (the FAIL marker) at program start --
! checked externally by the testbench exactly like every other program
! in this directory (xw_refill.strap, figure7_progressive_indexing.strap),
! not via the deck's own SIC/hang idiom.
!
! Discrimination, added after advisor review of an earlier version:
! checking only "RGZ fires after ones" / "RZ fires after zeros" cannot
! distinguish a correct implementation from one that sets RGZ and RZ
! identically (e.g. both always 1, or the two swapped) -- a bug that
! survives both single-direction checks can still make an assertion
! land on its expected marker by coincidence. Each load is therefore
! checked in BOTH directions: the indicator that SHOULD fire (X1/X2,
! matching WEN2/WEN's own choice) and the indicator that should NOT
! (X4/X5, not in the original source, added here specifically to rule
! out a swapped-indicator bug). X3 (VEN, a source-faithful duplicate of
! WEN2's own check) is kept as-is, matching the original's own
! apparent duplication, without an added inverse check of its own.
! Verified non-vacuous by deliberately swapping test 1's BRGZZ for
! BRZZ (the wrong indicator) and confirming the check then fails.

START   LVI, $1, 0.0        !X1 = 0 (fail marker: RGZ set after ones)
        LVI, $2, 0.0        !X2 = 0 (fail marker: RZ set after zeros)
        LVI, $3, 0.0        !X3 = 0 (fail marker: RGZ set after ones, again)
        LVI, $4, 0.0        !X4 = 0 (fail marker: RZ NOT set after ones)
        LVI, $5, 0.0        !X5 = 0 (fail marker: RGZ NOT set after zeros)

        L(BU,64,8), ONES    !WEN2 -LOAD ONES
        BRGZZ, T1AOK         !RGZ should be set (and gets cleared here)
        B, T1ADONE
T1AOK   LVI, $1, 100
T1ADONE BRZZ, T1BSKIP        !RZ should NOT be set -- branching here is the bug
        LVI, $4, 100         !RZ correctly not set
T1BSKIP L(BU,64,8), ZEROS   !WEN -LOAD ZEROS
        BRZZ, T2AOK          !RZ should be set (and gets cleared here)
        B, T2ADONE
T2AOK   LVI, $2, 100
T2ADONE BRGZZ, T2BSKIP       !RGZ should NOT be set -- branching here is the bug
        LVI, $5, 100         !RGZ correctly not set
T2BSKIP L(BU,64,8), ONES    !VEN
        BRGZZ, T3OK
        B, DONE
T3OK    LVI, $3, 100

DONE    BEW, $              !halt

ONES    DD(BU,64,8), 18446744073709551615   !0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF
ZEROS   DD(BU,64,8), 0

        END, START
